@@ -0,0 +1,25 @@
+# The Daily Grind
+
+Run `pnpm install`, then `pnpm start`. Set `PORT` to override port 11222.
+
+The server sends this HTTP response header to allow the app's origin to request
+resources on the user's local network and loopback interface:
+
+```http
+Permissions-Policy: local-network=(self), loopback-network=(self), local-network-access=(self)
+```
+
+The legacy `local-network-access` directive supports older browsers. Deployment
+hosts that serve the HTML directly must also send this header; a meta tag cannot
+configure Permissions Policy.
+
+Local requests require a secure context (HTTPS or localhost), browser permission,
+and appropriate CORS headers from the destination when reading cross-origin
+responses. If the app is embedded in a cross-origin iframe, the parent must also
+delegate these permissions using the iframe's `allow` attribute:
+
+```html
+allow="local-network; loopback-network; local-network-access"
+```
+
+See the [Local Network Access specification](https://wicg.github.io/local-network-access/).
